# Feature Factory context files — local only, never committed
.stargazer-*

# Agent worktrees (Claude Code `isolation: worktree`) — live INSIDE the repo,
# so without this they show as untracked and one `git add -A` stages entire
# checkouts. They also break a bare `npm test`: vitest's default glob collects
# every worktree's tests/, so the count reads N x the real suite (measured
# 2026-09-05: 1990 tests across 100 files, against a true 398 across 20).
# Scope a count with `npx vitest run --exclude '**/.claude/**'` while any
# worktree exists. Matches the convention already in ClaudeCode/.gitignore.
.claude/worktrees/
